        "kind": "proven",
        "exact": "1/6",
        "proofScope": "continuous",
        "source": "Emailed by NUE_13 #31 (generated by DeepSeek-V4-Pro, as disclosed): if one point lies inside the tetrahedron of the other four, the smallest volume is at most 1/12; otherwise the five points form a triangular bipyramid, the three crossing tetrahedra fill it exactly, and five points in the cube span at most 1/2, so the smallest volume is at most 1/6. A cube corner, its three neighbours and the opposite corner attain it. MinMax Arena supplied the Radon partition and the convexity of the hull volume. The optimum is exactly attainable on the nine-decimal grid.",
